      <problem>
        <p>Simplify: $$\left( {3\sqrt{2} - \sqrt{5}} \right)\left( {\sqrt{2} + 4\sqrt{5}} \right).$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step multiplication and simplification of two radical expressions, showing the progression from initial problem to final solution.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\mspace{72mu}\left( {3\sqrt{2} - \sqrt{5}} \right)\left( {\sqrt{2} + 4\sqrt{5}} \right)$$</cell>
